From: YSPEED firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] spi: mt7621: report transfer timeouts instead of discarding them

mt7621_spi_wait_till_ready() returns -ETIMEDOUT when the controller never
clears SPITRANS_BUSY, but every caller ignores the result, so transfer_one()
reports success to userspace even though no data was shifted. On the
YS-GPS-12832 that is indistinguishable from a working display bus.

Log the failure (rate limited) so a stalled controller shows up in dmesg
instead of looking like a successful transfer.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-mt7621.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-mt7621.c
@@ -154,6 +154,7 @@
 		udelay(1);
 	}
 
+	pr_err_ratelimited("spi-mt7621: transfer timeout, controller still busy\n");
 	return -ETIMEDOUT;
 }
 
